## Section 144 — Auditor not to render certain services

**Prohibited services (directly or indirectly)** to the company, its holding company or subsidiary:
1. accounting and book-keeping;
2. internal audit;
3. design and implementation of any financial information system;
4. actuarial services;
5. investment advisory services;
6. investment banking services;
7. outsourced financial services;
8. management services;
9. any other prescribed service.

**Other services.** Only such other services as are approved by the Board or the audit committee.

Board or audit committee approval cannot authorise a listed prohibited service. The bar protects independence under section 141.

This note is a focused study aid; the topic remains under source and current-law review.
